# The closed-socket tests (Test 46, Test 47 and the stalled-send variant) close
# the socket from the test thread while the handler's own thread is still inside
# write()/read() on that descriptor -- that is exactly the situation they exist
# to exercise ("the socket number was closed behind the handler's back").
# Product code never does this: disconnectImpl_() joins the receive thread
# before closesocket(), and sending and disconnecting both run on the single
# task thread. TSan's file-descriptor race detector therefore only sees the
race:testCloseSocket
